# The self-repair of .spun, built with SELF_REPAIR=1, through gui-test.py's
# proxy (@PORT@) to the test server. The .spun is copied into /dot by hand:
# spun.cat (@CAT@) has another app's line and none of its own. info of @APP@
# starts with the repair: .spun installs its own app, the alias spun, to the
# suggested /apps/wifi/spun with no question, and its zip's spun.dot
# overwrites C:/dot/spun. The release's version is the running .spun's, so
# info goes on. mame-repair.sh checks the commands sent, spun.cat and the
# files after the run.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
put @CAT@ /sys/spun.cat
autostart .spun -p @PORT@ info @APP@
autostart PRINT "SPUNREPAIRDONE"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 45
noreset 7.5
snap 15 21 25 30 44
screen 44 Repairing SPUN...
screen 44 Installed
screen 44 Next Test
screen 44 SPUNREPAIRDONE
